# Review before committing or pushing

When a feature, fix, or polish slice is finished:

1. Run the test suite (`npm test`) and relevant syntax or static checks to verify all changes pass.
2. Review `git status` and `git diff` to confirm only intended files are modified and no scratch or ignored data files (`public/data/c/*` outside `US`, `.env`, logs) are staged.
3. Present a concise summary of the changes and diffs to the user for review rather than automatically committing or pushing directly to `main`.
4. Only commit and push when explicitly asked, and never force-push `main`.
